  "unpairedEnglish": [
    {
      "section": "matins",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Hail, Queen of the Heavens! Hail, Mistress of earth! Hail, Virgin most pure of immaculate birth!",
          "pages": [
            383
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Clear star of the morning in beauty enshrined! O Lady make speed to the help of mankind.",
          "pages": [
            383
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Thee God in the depth of eternity chose; and formed thee all fair, as His glorious spouse;",
          "pages": [
            383
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "And called thee His Word’s own Mother to be, by Whom He created the earth, sky, and sea. Amen.",
          "pages": [
            384
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣. God elected her, and pre-elected her.",
          "pages": [
            384
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. He made her to dwell in His tabernacle.",
          "pages": [
            384
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "vespers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Hail, Dial of Achaz! On thee the true sun told backward the course which from old he had run!",
          "pages": [
            386
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "And, that man might be raised, submitting to shame, a little more low than the angels became.",
          "pages": [
            386
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Thou, rapt in the blaze of His infinite light, dost shine as the morn on the confines of night.",
          "pages": [
            386,
            387
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "As the moon on the lost through obscurity dawns; the serpent’s destroyer! A lily ’mid thorns! Amen.",
          "pages": [
            387
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣. I made an unfailing light to arise in heaven.",
          "pages": [
            387
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. And as a mist I overspread the whole earth.",
          "pages": [
            387
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "conclusion-of-the-hours",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣.. O Lady, aid my prayer.",
          "pages": [
            387
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. And let my cry come unto thee.",
          "pages": [
            387
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "Let us pray, Holy Mary, Queen of heaven, Mother of Our Lord Jesus Christ, and Mistress of the world, who forsakest no one and despisest no one, look upon me, O Lady, with an eye of pity and entreat for me, of thy beloved Son, the forgiveness of all my sins that, as I now celebrate, with devout affection, thy holy and immaculate conception, so here-after, I may receive the prize of eternal blessedness, by the grace of Him Whom thou, in virginity, didst bring forth, Jesus Christ our Lord: Who with the Father and the Holy Spirit, liveth and reigneth in perfect Trinity, God, forever. Amen.",
          "pages": [
            387,
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣. O Lady, aid my prayer",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. And let my cry come unto thee.",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣. Let us bless the Lord.",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. Thanks be to God.",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℣. May the souls of the faithful, through the mercy of God, rest in peace.",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "text": "℟. Amen.",
          "pages": [
            388
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
